.TH AVR\-TOKEN\-LIST 1 "" "avr 0.4.1" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-token-list \- List live tokens, newest first.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr token list
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List live tokens, newest first.
.PP
Shows your own tokens, or every member's when you are an organization admin. Revoked and expired tokens are not listed; `avr token view` still reads them by ID.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr token list
    avr token list --json id,name,expires_at
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    allow_vm_create, created_at, expires_at, grants, id, last_used_at,
    name, organization_id, revoked_at, revoked_reason, user_id,
    vm_create_count, vm_create_limit
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Max tokens to return. (default: 50)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-token (1),
.BR avr-token-create (1),
.BR avr-token-revoke (1),
.BR avr-token-view (1)
